each point has some fields
(x,y,enum are int and enum, they just need 4 bytes)
load icon has large size!

the idea is simple!
we just have some limited icon (cafe, hospital,...)
we can store them once, and reuse them!
instead repeat them on every point object!

1. so we move the cross field (icon field)
   to new class as "PointIcon" class
   (this is the object we want to share)
   we always need to separate it.

2. How we can sure, we are store each icon in a single place on memory?
   for this purpose, we create a factory class as "PointIconFactory "
   that guarantee this
   (if we have an icon of specific type, he return that icon
    if we hav not yet, he create it, store it, return it)

Note: factory class in this pattern always need
      "HASHMAP" data structure, because we tell him what icon we want
      he should check if there is?
      he want to find icon -----> value is icon
      based on icon type   -----> key is type


Note: flyweight object is an object that we can share
      like our PointIcon obj
                                                            flyweight class
      +------------------------+                    +------------------------------+
      |         Point          |------------------->|          PointIcon           |
      |------------------------|                    |------------------------------|
      | x : int                |                    | type : PointType             |
      | y : int                |                    | icon : byte[]                |
      +------------------------+                    +------------------------------+
                                                                    ^
                                                                    |
                                                                    |
      +------------------------+                    +------------------------------+
      |      PointService      |                    |       PointIconFactory       |
      |------------------------|. . . . . . .  . .> |------------------------------|
      | + getPoints()          |                    | + getPointIcon(type)         |
      +------------------------+                    |   : PointIcon                |
                                                    +------------------------------+



Summary:
         when we have repetitive objects
         we can use the flyweight pattern
         we need separate the data we want to share
         store it somewhere else (like factory class)

